  message: "2026-06-10 design-interview ruling (ADR-0041, merged in PR #4181): tier 2 = workspace-internal only, and the stdlib/third_party distinction moves to a separate ecosystem axis — giving the classifier an unambiguous boundary for workspace and first-party source. Stays violated until the classifier conforms; re-validate after the implementation lands."  # 071a
- op: discuss  # ead5
  at: '2026-06-26T22:26:29Z'  # ead5
  by: agent  # ead5
  actor: jgstern_agent  # ead5
  clock: 10  # ead5
  nonce: ead5  # ead5
  message: "supply-verdict:F3 (workspace-member subtraction) landed in PR #4316 (dev 446959478b) — the FIRST of INV-nuzas's two halves; item stays violated pending F4.\n\nWhat F3 fixed: parse_python_dependencies stamped every resolved import name from every pyproject's [project].dependencies as {direct: True} (-> tier 2). In a monorepo, sibling packages declare each other as deps, so a package's own first-party code landed in the dependency manifest and the boundary classifier stamped it as an EXTERNAL tier-2 'direct dependency' (the reason=direct-dependency face of this item). F3 reads each package's OWN distribution name ([project].name / [tool.poetry].name via new _extract_distribution_name) and subtracts it from the resolved import set after the stdlib carve-out.\n\nBehavioral evidence (self-analysis on the hypergumbo monorepo, 8 pyproject files, direct parse_python_dependencies() call): hypergumbo_* sibling packages in the tier-2 manifest 5 -> 0 (hypergumbo_core, hypergumbo_lang_common, hypergumbo_lang_extended1, hypergumbo_lang_mainstream, hypergumbo_lang_rust_analyzer all removed); 7 workspace own-names subtracted; 91 genuine third-party entries retained. Those 5 top-level manifest entries are what stamped this item's ~144 hypergumbo_* submodule boundary nodes tier-2-direct, so all of them are de-classified off the manifest. Production-path test: TestWorkspaceMemberSubtraction in test_py_deps.py (workspace sibling subtracted, third-party retained, poetry-name variant).\n\nREMAINING (F4, the second half): in-tree module resolution so hypergumbo_* imports resolve to real in-repo nodes instead of becoming boundary nodes at all (py.py import resolver, ~py.py:2004-2022). Until F4, the de-manifested siblings fall to tier-3 generic-external rather than tier-2-direct (less wrong, still not in-repo). F4 closes INV-nuzas. Note: orthogonal to the tier-2-vs-tier-3 reassignment of genuine third-party deps (supply-verdict:F5 / ADR-0041 section 1, NOT touched here)."  # ead5
- op: discuss  # 333f
  at: '2026-06-27T08:08:41Z'  # 333f
  by: agent  # 333f
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 333f
  clock: 11  # 333f
  nonce: 333f  # 333f
  message: "supply-verdict:F4 (in-tree module resolution) landed in dev ba11d947a5 — the IMPORT half of INV-nuzas is now closed; item stays violated on a distinct call-edge residual (below).\n\nWhat F4 fixed (producer-side, py.py only): the analyzer now builds a module_to_file_id map (every in-tree dotted module name -> its first-party file-anchor id, plus the package name per __init__.py) and _extract_import_edges resolves to it. Two import forms that previously dangled to phantom external_symbol boundary nodes now resolve to the real first-party file node (is_resolved=True, no ExternalRef): (A) ast.Import 'import pkg.sub.mod' (which did zero symbol lookup); (B) ast.ImportFrom 'from pkg import submod' where submod is a submodule, not a re-exported symbol. The existing symbol lookup still wins first (precise symbol targets unchanged); genuine third-party stays external (absent from the map).\n\nBehavioral evidence (self-analysis on the hypergumbo monorepo, hypergumbo run . , before->after):\n- imports edges mis-routed to python:hypergumbo_* phantom externals: 366 -> 0 (symptom 2's import-routing defect, fully closed).\n- hypergumbo_* modules mislabelled internal_dep ('direct dependency (pyproject.toml)'): 144 -> 0 (symptom 1; internal_dep symbol count 480 -> 176).\n- phantom hypergumbo_* external_symbol nodes: 331 -> 116 (65% reduction).\n\nREMAINING (keeps this violated): the residual 116 phantom hypergumbo_* externals are reached ONLY by calls (339) and module_attr_ref (106) edges -- ZERO imports edges. These are cross-module CALL/reference-resolution failures (e.g. 'from x import fn; fn()' -> fn :unresolved; 'mod.ATTR.values' module_attr_ref), a DISTINCT mechanism from import resolution, owned by WI-noham (obj.method()/short-name -> :unresolved) + dispatch:F3 (Python alias/builtin/reference resolution, currently blocked on the py.py scope-stack rewrite). INV-nuzas's own proposed acceptance property ('no external_symbol canonical_name starts with a workspace prefix') still fails on these 116, so the invariant is not yet satisfied. Suggest: when WI-noham/dispatch:F3 land, re-measure and close INV-nuzas; or split the call-edge facet onto WI-noham and close INV-nuzas on the import facet (human call).\n\nScope-outs (stated, not hidden): PEP-420 namespace package bare 'import nspkg' (no __init__.py) has no file anchor for the package name and stays external (a submodule 'import nspkg.mod' of a real file does resolve). Cross-language analogues (Go/Java/Kotlin in-tree module imports) filed separately. Tagged awaits_bakeoff_validation (quantitative claim)."  # 333f
